[Music]  my name is matty van truyon  and we are in feral scotland  i'm a crafter and a knitter  i design feral garments and i sell them  online  [Music]  [Applause]  fedele is known  in the world as a knitting technique  that involves stranded collar knitting  so it's basically carrying two colors  together in one row sometimes three  it's called fair isle because originated  here in the island  the shetland wool was known for being  one of the softest wolves in the world  fair isle belongs to the shetland  islands  the population of ship is a lot higher  than the human population  [Music]  the making of a feral jumper i think it  can be divided in two different  processes one is the husbandry of the  animals and then the other one is the  making of the garment  you have a flock of sheep looking after  them feeding them make sure that they  stay healthy so that you produce a good  fleece  [Music]  shearing i found that the best way to do  it is by allowing the ship to rest on  your legs  they become very dose island kind of  happy animals  the moment that becomes like a factory  thing then the relationship changes  completely  [Music]  the fleece is spread out you clean any  debris any grass you roll it in one  little bundle  then it's sent out to jameson spinning  in mainland shetland with the good  shepherd  they're sorted and they're graded  according to the quality of the wool  then they get processed  it gets washed it gets sort of pulled  apart dyed spun  twisted and then we get the cones  [Music]  the cones get sent normally with the  aeroplane from tin wool into fetal  i received my yarn with the plane i got  collected and bring it to my studio and  then the process of making the garment  begins  it comes the design stage i start  putting together colors and patterns and  i create swatches  once the design is approved then we go  into the detailing  the knitting process starts with  producing the ribs taking that drip  transferring it into the flatbed  knitting machine  i place all my wools and then i start  knitting the garment  the machine reads the solid and hollow  front back right sleeve left sleeve  all these panels get put together  the sleeve gets attached by a technical  grafting creates an invisible thing  the seam gets sewn along the sleeve  [Music]  i produce the neck and then the neck  gets grafted into the garment  once the garment is nature is the  finishing process  trimming all the insides you have to  weave in the ends it's the moment where  i can check if there's been any mistake  on the weavings  the garment gets washed in 30 degrees  temperature  put it on the stretcher in the woolly  horse to dry  [Music]  once it's dry it gets pressed unlabeled  it's normally wrapped in brown paper  parcel kind of old style with a little  string of wood  the knitting belongs to the island  people stop doing it they leave the  island and someone else comes and  carries on so feeling that i'm  continuing a tradition and preserving a  heritage is full of satisfaction  [Music]  you

